A||||9||Raydar||Power window wiring harness?||||5||
Z||000000||Raydar||01-21-2000||12:49 PM||||Do the 88 cars, specifically the Formula, have the power window harness installed as part of the standard wiring? Or is it a separate harness?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||01-21-2000||01:34 PM||||I'm pretty sure all power window harnesses are wrapped in the sheithing with the cross car harness.  I just pulled one out of an 86.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||01-21-2000||01:57 PM||||If the Formula has the power window harness already installed I couldn't find it when I converted mine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||01-21-2000||03:32 PM||||The only harness I have ever seen that was there when the car was not equiped with the option was the trunk release. But any of the stuff is easy to install. I now have every option available on my car including the vanity mirror on both visors||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||01-21-2000||05:52 PM||||Okay, maybe it was specific to an 86. Friend of mine just parted out an 86. SE, I think.  Didn't have power windows, but had the plugs, under the console, and apparently the rest of the harness. My 88 coupe didn't. Thanks, guys!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||01-21-2000||06:07 PM||||Maybe someone unpowered his windows in the past??? <P>Could be an assembly line screw up too.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||01-21-2000||06:11 PM||||I'm getting an '85 GT with p/windows.  Will it also have the wiring for p/mirrors?  I know it's a separate harness, but is it there?  I already have the p/mirror heads although I just gave away the switch and mounting console.  I don't need p/mirrors as I'm the only one driving my Fiero (too low for my wife and I wouldn't trust many others) but they would still be cool to have.||||reg||1
Z||000008||David Gamache||01-23-2000||05:07 PM||||The power window wire harness is a seperate harness. The power window harness came with or without the power door lock option. Just as the power mirrors or subwolfer wire harness is seperate. The 85-early 86 harnesses were almost the same as 87-88 except for the earlier harnesses had different plug connectors on the power mirror harness and an additional pin switch. As far as I remember the power window harnesses were the same 85-up. If you need a particular harness let me know and we could probably work out a reasonable deal. i have just about everything imaginable buried somewhere in the garage, possibly even the lost ARK.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||01-25-2000||04:42 PM||||So are you saying that, if my '85 GT has p/l (which is does, I think), I also have the p/m harness?  I have a pair of good p/m heads and I think I could locate the rest of the stuff (Hey, Tom!).||||reg||1
Z||000010||David Gamache||01-26-2000||12:57 AM||||If your car has p/locks it may have p/ window wires, but the p/mirror harness is seperate. Behind the kick panels by the floor lights is a large flat plug that holds, I believe up to 5 wires if all the plug spots are filled the car is wired for p/l and p/w if there are only 2 or three, I don't remember off the top of my head,then the car is wired for locks only. the p/m harness has a plug, when the car is so equipped, that is a small square plug that houses 4 wires. the plug is a clear color on earlier models and black on later models.   ||||reg||1
